Let me work through this step by step.

First, the low cloud at the solar horizon sits at 68 percent, which is above the 60 percent
blocking threshold, so the low sun is unlikely to reach the underside of the mid-level deck.
Second, the far-field sample at 226 km is also at 71 percent, so this reads as an extensive
blanket rather than a thin strip — no softening of the penalty is warranted.

Third, the aerosol proxy shows AOD 0.11 with PM2.5 at 8 micrograms per cubic metre, which is
clean maritime air: no dust warmth to add, but no smoke haze to subtract either.

On balance I would call this a poor evening for colour and a mediocre one for golden hour.
